Package: cdrgam
Title: Continuous-Time Deconvolution Using Generalized Additive Models
Version: 0.1.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Cory", "Shain", , "cory.shain@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2704-7197"))
Author: Cory Shain [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Cory Shain <cory.shain@gmail.com>
Description: Fits continuous-time deconvolutional regression models as
    generalized additive models. Response-level spline designs are computed
    from irregularly sampled impulse histories in bounded-memory chunks,
    then fitted with either 'mgcv' or custom dense and sparse backends.
    Custom backends provide Gaussian restricted maximum likelihood and
    Poisson, binomial, and Gamma Laplace marginal-likelihood fitting.
    Fitted objects provide standard model methods and retain their translated
    'mgcv' representation.
